    recipeInstructions: [
      'Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onions, green bell pepper, and red bell pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, about 5 minutes.',
      'Add the jalapeños and garlic. Cook, stirring, for 1 minute.',
      'Add the chili powder, cumin, oregano, cayenne, salt, and black pepper. Stir to coat the vegetables and cook for 1 minute.',
      'Add the canned crushed tomatoes, kidney beans, pinto beans, sweet corn, and vegetable stock. Stir to combine.',
      'Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low. Simmer uncovered for 25–30 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the chili thickens.',
      'Taste and adjust seasoning. Serve hot.',
      'Suggestions (not included): Top with shredded cheese, sour cream, sliced avocado, or fresh cilantro. Serve with cornbread or tortilla chips.'
    ],
