    recipeInstructions: [
      'Pour the buttermilk into a shallow bowl. Add the shrimp and soak for 10 minutes, turning once.',
      'In a separate shallow dish, whisk together the flour, salt, black pepper, garlic powder, paprika, and cayenne pepper until evenly combined.',
      'Lift each shrimp from the buttermilk, letting the excess drip off, then dredge in the seasoned flour, pressing lightly to adhere. Shake off the excess and set on a clean plate.',
      'Pour 1½ to 2 inches of vegetable oil into a large heavy skillet or Dutch oven and heat to 375°F (190°C). The ingredient list shows the oil absorbed into the shrimp; use enough additional oil to maintain frying depth.',
      'Working in batches to avoid crowding, carefully lower the shrimp into the hot oil. Fry for 2–3 minutes, turning once halfway through, until golden brown and cooked through.',
      'Use a slotted spoon or spider to transfer the fried shrimp to a paper towel-lined plate. Allow the oil to return to 375°F between batches.',
      'Repeat with the remaining shrimp. Serve immediately for maximum crispness.',
      'Suggestions (not included): Serve with cocktail sauce, tartar sauce, or lemon wedges. Pairs well with coleslaw or french fries.'
    ],
