    recipeInstructions: [
      'Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add 1 tsp of table salt per quart of water after it boils, then add the dry pasta. Cook 8 minutes (al dente). Reserve ½ cup pasta water, then drain and set aside.',
      'Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the garlic and cook 30 seconds until fragrant.',
      'Add the broccoli, asparagus, and bell pepper. Sauté 3–4 minutes until beginning to soften.',
      'Add the zucchini and cook 2 minutes more. Stir in the peas and cherry tomatoes. Cook 1 minute.',
      'Pour in the white wine and cook until mostly evaporated, about 2 minutes.',
      'Add the drained pasta and a splash of pasta water. Toss well. Stir in the lemon juice and Parmesan until the sauce coats the pasta, adding more pasta water as needed.',
      'Remove from heat. Fold in the basil. Season with salt, pepper, and more lemon juice to taste.',
      'Divide among 4 plates and serve immediately with extra Parmesan.',
      'Suggestions (not included): Top with toasted pine nuts. Use any combination of seasonal vegetables you like.'
    ],
